    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "Asking \"And you?\" with 呢",
      "body": "After you say something about yourself, you can turn the same question back to the other person. Just put 呢 after a person word: 你呢？ means \"And you?\" or \"What about you?\". The listener knows what you're asking from what you just said.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "zh": "我是学生，你呢？",
          "en": "I'm a student. And you?"
        },
